<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d158bfc01d38> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Complaints about the company's latest hardware revision, called AP2, have been made by drivers for many months, often claiming that they felt the system was not as accurate as the company's first iteration, AP1." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "173" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d1979f55cbbd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) determined that a “lack of safeguards” contributed to Brown’s death." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d26806787e3c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In August, Reuters reported that Tesla removed a Chinese term for “self-driving” from its China website after a driver in Beijing had a nonfatal crash while Autopilot was engaged." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd97f39d0f89> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company sells a version of Autopilot called “Full Self-Driving,” even though drivers are consistently warned to keep their hands on the steering wheel and eyes on the road when operating it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e25399210222> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1558] The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) determined that a “lack of safeguards” contributed to Brown’s death." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f1a6b99228e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver’s father, Gao Jubin, told CCTV he thought his son had been relying on Autopilot to drive the car and so was not watching the road when the crash took place." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

