<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/46bed479210b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla Motors came under renewed questioning about the safety of its Autopilot technology after news emerged on Wednesday of a fatal crash in China that may have occurred while the automated driver-assist system was operating." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b8b6f6707c39> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Complaints about the company's latest hardware revision, called AP2, have been made by drivers for many months, often claiming that they felt the system was not as accurate as the company's first iteration, AP1." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "173" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6ba555132892> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The crash took place on Jan. 20 and killed Gao Yaning, 23, when the Tesla Model S he was driving slammed into a road sweeper on a highway near Handan, a city about 300 miles south of Beijing, according to a report broadcast on Wednesday by the Chinese government news channel CCTV." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/743aae4cb318> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "News of the China crash comes just three days after Tesla’s chief executive, Elon Musk, outlined changes planned for Autopilot that he said would have prevented Mr. Brown’s accident and that he contended would make the Model S one of the safest cars on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f1fba522849> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the National Transportation Safety Board (NTSB) states in a report released on Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9fe6eacdd7d5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) determined that a “lack of safeguards” contributed to Brown’s death." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e0f30e7b8f06> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla CEO Elon Musk has been criticized for overstating the autonomous capabilities of his vehicles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f6ef6c126fbb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Although Tesla learned of the Florida accident a few weeks after it happened, it did not publicly disclose it until late June, when the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration announced it was investigating the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7677880f75a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“We are hoping Tesla, when marketing its products, will be more cautious. Don’t just use self-driving as a selling point for young people.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1559" .

